    "probe_text": "I've traced the full pipeline in `owners.POST.yml` and read each function class. Here is what actually happens, in execution order.\n\n## Precondition (whole endpoint)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. The entire endpoint is guarded; a caller lacking that role never reaches step one.\n\n## Idempotency short-circuit\n1. **`CheckIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header. If absent \u2192 continue normally. If present and *previously seen* \u2192 takes the `replay` branch: **`LoadReplayedOwner`** loads the original owner and **`RespondWithOwner`** returns it (200), *bypassing all validation and creation below*. If present but new \u2192 falls through (recorded later, after save).\n\n## Validations (in order, each a 400/409/429 before anything is built or saved)\n2. **`ValidateOwnerFields`** *(validation + side-effect)* \u2014 first canonicalizes the address in place via `OwnerAddress.normalizeInto` (prefers `addressLine1/2`, else flat `address`; writes the composed value back to `address`). Then requires **firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone** to be non-null/non-blank \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException`. Republishes the body as a variable for later steps.\n3. **`NormalizeOwnerTelephone`** *(validation + side-effect)* \u2014 converts telephone to E.164; a number that can't form valid E.164 \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException`. Mutates the DTO to the E.164 value.\n4. **`NormalizeOwnerEmail`** *(validation + side-effect)* \u2014 email optional; if present must be syntactically valid \u2192 else `InvalidEmailException`; stored **lower-cased** (mutates DTO). Null/blank left untouched.\n5. **`RejectDisposableEmail`** *(validation)* \u2014 if email present and its domain is on the disposable blocklist \u2192 `DisposableEmailException`. No mutation.\n6. **`ValidateOwnerPostcode`** *(validation)* \u2014 postcode optional; if present must be **exactly 4 digits**, and for a city with a known region must fall within that region's range \u2192 else `InvalidPostcodeException`. Unknown-region city accepts any 4 digits. Value unchanged.\n7. **`ValidateRegistrationDate`** *(validation)* \u2014 registrationDate optional; if supplied it must not be after `LocalDate.now()` \u2192 else `FutureRegistrationDateException`.\n8. **`EnsureUniqueIdentity`** *(validation)* \u2014 hard duplicate block: computes `householdId` from `(lastName, postcode)`; if any non-deleted existing owner already has that household \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409). Skipped when `sharesHousehold=true` or when there's no postcode.\n9. **`EnsureCityCapacity`** *(validation)* \u2014 if the city (counted case-insensitively) already holds \u2265 **50** owners \u2192 `CityCapacityExceededException` (409).\n\n## Resolve date, then final gate\n10. **`ResolveRegistrationDate`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 computes effective date = supplied date else today, then **rolls a weekend forward to the next business day**; publishes it as a `LocalDate` variable.\n11. **`EnsureDailyLimit`** *(validation)* \u2014 if \u2265 **100** owners are already registered on that resolved business day \u2192 `DailyLimitExceededException` (429).\n\n## Build and stamp the owner (all mutate the built entity in place, pre-save)\n12. **`BuildOwner`** \u2014 maps the DTO to a new `Owner` via `OwnerMapper`.\n13. **`ApplyRegistrationDate`** \u2014 stamps the resolved business-day date onto the owner, overwriting whatever the mapper set.\n14. **`AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode; HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex chars of SHA-256(telephone + lastName)), **de-duplicated** by appending `-<n>` if it collides with an existing owner's code.\n15. **`AssignMembershipNumber`** \u2014 sets `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` comes from `FiscalYear.shortLabel(registrationDate)` \u2014 i.e. the **fiscal** year (note: the YAML comment says \"registration date year\", but the code uses fiscal year).\n16. **`AssignHousehold`** \u2014 sets `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256(lastName, postcode); unset when there's no postcode.\n17. **`AssignHouseholdSize`** \u2014 sets `householdSize` = existing members sharing the `householdId` + 1.\n18. **`AssignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing this first+last name (case-insensitive; excludes the new owner since it isn't saved yet).\n19. **`AssignPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 soft-duplicate flag: if a non-deleted existing owner shares last name (case-insensitive) + non-blank postcode but has a *different* telephone, sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf=<that id>` (first match wins); otherwise false/null. Always false/null when `sharesHousehold=true`.\n\n## Persist and post-save side-effects\n20. **`SaveOwner`** \u2014 persists the owner (assigns its generated id).\n21. **`RecordIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 if the request carried an `Idempotency-Key`, records `key \u2192 owner.id` in the store so future repeats replay this owner.\n22. **`AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 logs to the `AUDIT` logger: owner id, customerCode, registrationDate, `MembershipLevel.of(owner)`, and membershipNumber.\n23. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto`, additionally **sets `bulkSignupWarning` from `BulkSignup.warningRaised(repo)`** on the DTO (a side-effect not mentioned in the YAML comments), and returns **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Notes / cross-checks worth flagging\n- **Transaction scope:** every step from `ensureUniqueIdentity` onward (and the replay branch) declares `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the reads-for-uniqueness and the write commit as one transaction at the end. The early validation/normalization steps (2\u20137, 10) run *outside* the transaction.\n- **All eight \"gates\"** run strictly before `BuildOwner`, so no owner is constructed or saved when any validation fails \u2014 matching the file's intent.\n- **`membershipNumber` uses fiscal year**, not calendar year \u2014 a genuine mismatch between the YAML comment and `AssignMembershipNumber`/`FiscalYear`.\n- **Membership level (GOLD) is not stored** by a pipeline step; it's derived on the fly (`MembershipLevel.of(owner)`, from `householdSize`) in audit and DTO mapping. The YAML comment about the responder \"promoting\" the household to GOLD overstates it \u2014 the responder doesn't set it; it's computed from the stored `householdSize`.\n\nI didn't change anything."
